+# Local Aurora water extension (experimental fork)
+
+These API lines are deliberately incompatible with stock Horizon. They are local
+experiments on base `1f3ccb0fc3e593a6fe3a3c7da76d8e3d620e5b6d`, not an upstream
+compatibility promise. No code from other shader packs or renderers was used.
+
+`0.1-aurora-water.1` adds semantic `MaterialInput.is_water` via a spare terrain
+vertex bit, preserving the 24-byte vertex layout. The fluid mesher tags water
+(including waterlogged fluid), not glass, ice, lava or modelled cauldron water.
+This first extension also adds the field to the local 0.1 prelude: packs that
+construct MaterialInput themselves need adaptation.
+
+`0.1-aurora-water.2` opts a material stage into a separate pre-translucent scene
+capture. Other API lines do not allocate its targets or execute its pass. Its
+material prelude adds:
+
+- `MaterialInput.screen_uv`: fragment pixel centre divided by world resolution;
+  top-left origin. Actual raster coordinates, including jitter.
+- `MaterialInput.fog`: RGB native fog colour, alpha the exact fog mix factor at
+  the current surface, combining native spherical and cylindrical fog ranges.
+- Group 3 binding 1: `pre_translucent_color: texture_2d<f32>`.
+- Binding 2: `pre_translucent_depth: texture_depth_2d`, reversed, 0 for sky.
+- Binding 3: `scene_sampler`, linear/clamp-to-edge.
+- `pre_translucent_depth_at(uv)`: a clamped nearest depth load.
+- `Surface(color, scene_composited)`: false retains normal alpha test/blend/fog;
+  true skips native fog **only in the translucent fragment**. Use it for a fully
+  composited colour, normally alpha 1. Do not fog the captured background twice.
+
+The frame stays at binding 0. For a scene-enabled pack its projection matrices
+match the current world pass, including TAA jitter, bob and spin. The camera-
+relative world position follows from inverse projection, perspective divide,
+then inverse view with w=0.
+
+Snapshot resources are valid **only in translucent terrain**, after capture in
+this frame. Never read them in the solid material stage. No snapshot resources
+are added to sky/post. The additional constructors are opt-in to water.2; water.1
+and the previously extended 0.1 prelude do not change again.
+
+The renderer ends the world pass before translucent terrain, copies colour and
+Depth32Float through a fullscreen render pass into separate sampled attachments,
+then resumes the world with Load operations and rebound groups/index buffers.
+The material never samples its active render attachments. Source binding and
+snapshot targets are refreshed on resize or world-target replacement. Dropping
+the material releases the snapshot.
+
+This is not a pure opaque-only scene: earlier weather, items and effects are
+included. Transparent terrain, later particles and clouds are absent. It cannot
+resolve arbitrary transparent layers or reconstruct off-screen/occluded colour.
+At BGRA8 + Depth32Float the two images cost 8 bytes per world pixel, excluding
+alignment/driver overhead (28.1 MiB at 2560×1440). Measure total GPU frame time;
+this capture is not yet a separate item in the pack's pass-timing overlay.
+
+The renderer test `gfx::native_scene::tests::snapshot_is_independent_fresh_and_resized`
+checks real colour/depth pixels, source mutation after capture, a new frame and
+resize. It reports an explicit skip when no GPU is available; that is not GPU
+validation. Test the actual game with both sky/material stages (their group 3
+layouts differ), material-only/TAA, hot reload, resize and a previous API pack.
+Use disposable homes/worlds as required by AGENTS.md.
-- 
